corrections.original:
Four threads each increment their own element of a shared array 100 million times. On 4 cores this runs **slower** than doing all the work in one thread. Why?

```c
long counts[4];

void *work(void *arg) {
    int me = *(int *)arg;
    for (long i = 0; i < 100000000;
         i++)
        counts[me]++;
    return NULL;
}
```

